OL,3,GFEATURES CNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FWomen were also making their mark in
OL,7,Fother areas of factual broadcasting
OL,8,Faround the same time.
OL,10,FIn 1975 Sue Lawley was the main
OL,11,Fpresenter of the Tonight programme (the
OL,12,Fancestor of Newsnight) before she
OL,13,Freturned to Nationwide.
OL,15,FValerie Singleton also demonstrated
OL,16,Fthat she could leave her Blue Peter
OL,17,Fimage behind on Nationwide and, later,
OL,18,FThe Money Programme although she still
OL,19,Fappeared occasionally on BP on special
OL,20,Foccasions.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,134,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13306
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F133A1768767025
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FMeanwhile Barbara Edwards was also
OL,7,Fmaking history even if she was billed
OL,8,Fin Radio Times as the "weatherman".
OL,10,FSo with all this in mind, it seems
OL,11,Fsurprising in hindsight that it was
OL,12,Fstill unusual to hear women network
OL,13,Fannouncers.
OL,15,FSome were tried out on attachment ` but
OL,16,Fmostly filled the daytime shifts, often
OL,17,Fon BBC Two where they had little to do
OL,18,Fapart from read the Service Information
OL,19,Fbulletin and link into Play School.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,134,120,200,300,0,100
